      "id": "s0143",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Cancelling"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0144",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "StatusDetails -> (string)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0145",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A detailed status of the command execution for an invocation. [[p0]] includes more information than [[p1]] because it includes states resulting from error and concurrency control parameters. [[p2]] can show different results than [[p3]] . For more information about these statuses, see [[p4]] in the [[p5]]Amazon Web Services Systems Manager User Guide[[p6]] . [[p7]] can be one of the following values:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "StatusDetails"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "Status"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "StatusDetails"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "Status"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "Understanding command statuses"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p6]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p7]]",
          "text": "StatusDetails"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0146",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pending: The command hasn’t been sent to the managed node.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0147",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "In Progress: The command has been sent to the managed node but hasn’t reached a terminal state.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0148",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Delayed: The system attempted to send the command to the target, but the target wasn’t available. The managed node might not be available because of network issues, because the node was stopped, or for similar reasons. The system will try to send the command again.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0149",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Success: The command or plugin ran successfully. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0150",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Delivery Timed Out: The command wasn’t delivered to the managed node before the delivery timeout expired. Delivery timeouts don’t count against the parent command’s [[p0]] limit, but they do contribute to whether the parent command status is Success or Incomplete. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "MaxErrors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0151",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Execution Timed Out: The command started to run on the managed node, but the execution wasn’t complete before the timeout expired. Execution timeouts count against the [[p0]] limit of the parent command. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "MaxErrors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0152",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Failed: The command wasn’t run successfully on the managed node. For a plugin, this indicates that the result code wasn’t zero. For a command invocation, this indicates that the result code for one or more plugins wasn’t zero. Invocation failures count against the [[p0]] limit of the parent command. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "MaxErrors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0153",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Cancelled: The command was terminated before it was completed. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0154",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Undeliverable: The command can’t be delivered to the managed node. The node might not exist or might not be responding. Undeliverable invocations don’t count against the parent command’s [[p0]] limit and don’t contribute to whether the parent command status is Success or Incomplete. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "MaxErrors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0155",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Terminated: The parent command exceeded its [[p0]] limit and subsequent command invocations were canceled by the system. This is a terminal state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "MaxErrors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0156",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Constraints:",
      "protected": []
